{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "flatten_registry_order",
    "description": "esm-spec §9.6.4 rule 7 / §10.7 / esm-libraries-spec §4.7.5 step 4: the merged registry's ORDER. Components are declared out of alphabetical order (Zulu, Alpha, Mike) and their authored entries are not alphabetical (Zulu: s, aa; Mike: aa, s); Zulu also materializes two imported entries (lib_z, lib_a), which follow its authored entries sorted by UTF-8 bytes. The merge walks components in document order, each block as emit materializes it: `s` collides (Zulu and Mike carry f+1, Alpha f+2), so Zulu and Mike share ONE entry named after the first owner in document order, `Zulu.s`, and Alpha gets `Alpha.s`; `aa` is deep-equal everywhere and kept once under its bare name.",
    "authors": [
      "out-of-line-expression-templates conformance"
    ]
  },
